[00:00.39]Lesson 9 | 第9课
[00:02.28]Royal Espionage | 王室谍报
[00:11.31]What important thing did King Alfred learn when he penetrated the Danish camp of Guthrum? | 阿尔弗雷德国王潜入古特伦的丹麦营地时，了解到什么重要情况？
[00:20.72]Alfred the Great acted as his own spy, visiting Danish camps disguised as a minstrel. | 阿尔弗雷德大帝亲自充当间谍，乔装成吟游诗人，前往丹麦人的营地。
[00:29.54]In those days wandering minstrels were welcome everywhere. | 在那个时代，四处游历的吟游诗人到处都受到欢迎。
[00:34.45]They were not fighting men, and their harp was their passport. | 他们不是战士，而竖琴就是他们通行无阻的凭证。
[00:39.20]Alfred had learned many of their ballads in his youth and could vary his programme with acrobatic tricks and simple conjuring. | 阿尔弗雷德年轻时学会了许多吟游诗人的民谣，还会表演杂技和简单的戏法，使节目更加丰富。
[00:49.17]While Alfred's little army slowly began to gather at Athelney, the king himself set out to penetrate the camp of Guthrum, the commander of the Danish invaders. | 当阿尔弗雷德的小部队开始在阿瑟尔尼逐渐集结时，国王亲自出发，潜入丹麦入侵军指挥官古特伦的营地。
[01:02.26]These had settled down for the winter at Chippenham: thither Alfred went. | 丹麦人已在奇彭纳姆安顿下来过冬，阿尔弗雷德便前往那里。
[01:09.32]He noticed at once that discipline was slack: the Danes had the self-confidence of conquerors, and their security precautions were casual. | 他立刻注意到，丹麦人的纪律十分松懈：他们具有征服者的自信，安全防范措施也很随意。
[01:21.06]They lived well, on the proceeds of raids on neighbouring regions. | 他们靠掠夺邻近地区所得的财物过着优裕的生活。
[01:26.77]There they collected women as well as food and drink, and a life of ease had made them soft. | 他们在那里掳掠妇女，搜集食物和饮料；安逸的生活已经使他们变得软弱。
[01:34.89]Alfred stayed in the camp a week before he returned to Athelney. | 阿尔弗雷德在营地待了一周，然后才返回阿瑟尔尼。
[01:40.13]The force there assembled was trivial compared with the Danish horde. | 在那里集结的部队与丹麦大军相比，人数少得微不足道。
[01:45.12]But Alfred had deduced that the Danes were no longer fit for prolonged battle: and that their commissariat had no organization, but depended on irregular raids. | 但阿尔弗雷德推断，丹麦人已不再适合打持久战，而且他们的军需供应毫无组织可言，只能依靠不定期的劫掠。
[01:58.52]So, faced with the Danish advance, Alfred did not risk open battle but harried the enemy. | 因此，面对丹麦人的进攻，阿尔弗雷德没有冒险与敌人正面交战，而是不断袭扰他们。
[02:06.57]He was constantly on the move, drawing the Danes after him. | 他不断转移位置，引诱丹麦人跟在自己后面。
[02:11.58]His patrols halted the raiding parties: hunger assailed the Danish army. | 他的巡逻队阻截了丹麦人的劫掠队伍，丹麦军队开始陷入饥荒。
[02:17.97]Now Alfred began a long series of skirmishes—and within a month the Danes had surrendered. | 随后，阿尔弗雷德开始了一系列持续不断的小规模战斗；不到一个月，丹麦人便投降了。
[02:25.74]The episode could reasonably serve as a unique epic of royal espionage! | 这一事件完全可以称得上是一段独特的王室间谍传奇！